From 5548d384b663de2b997261db765cb370e12cf0a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:35:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm/filogic/mtk_wmac: WF top IP version 0x02060000 on
 MT7981 too

The mt7915 driver polls the WF top's IP version (0x184b0010) for
0x02060000 before it starts the WM CPU and, right after, stores the a-die
SKU in CONNINFRA_SKU_DEC.  The model answered MT7981 with the CONN_INFRA
version 0x02090000 (and MT7986 with 0): the poll timed out silently,
mt7986_wmac_enable() returned before the SKU update, the driver did not
see the MT7976 a-die, read the TX power from the MT7915 EEPROM offsets
and got 0: 3 dBm on a Cudy WR3000P.  Now 20 dBm as in its calibration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/arm/filogic/mtk_wmac.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/arm/filogic/mtk_wmac.c b/hw/arm/filogic/mtk_wmac.c
index 75860dd..0d20af1 100644
--- a/hw/arm/filogic/mtk_wmac.c
+++ b/hw/arm/filogic/mtk_wmac.c
@@ -365,7 +365,13 @@ static uint64_t wmac_read(void *opaque, hwaddr addr, unsigned size)
             v = s->sku ? rget(s->regs, a) : 0x02090000;     /* MT7981 */
             break;
         case WF_TOP_CFG_IP_VER:
-            v = s->sku ? rget(s->regs, a) : 0x02090000;
+            /*
+             * the WF top's own IP version (MT7981 and MT7986 alike): the
+             * driver polls for it before the WM CPU starts and only then
+             * stores the a-die SKU (CONNINFRA_SKU_DEC) that selects the
+             * MT7976 EEPROM layout - with another value TX power reads 0
+             */
+            v = 0x02060000;
             break;
         case WF_TOP_ROMCODE_INDEX:
             v = 0x1d1e;
